Issue 1 is ready for your review. I changed only the comment in [common.go](/Users/peter/code/devenv/cli/cmd/entire/cli/strategy/common.go:125) so it now explicitly says divergence still updates the local ref, instead of implying all non-rewind cases are preserved.

Verification:
- `go test ./cmd/entire/cli -run '^TestFetchMetadataBranch_DoesNotRewindLocalAhead$'`
- `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy -run '^TestFetchV2MainFromURL_DoesNotRewindLocalAhead$|^TestFetchMetadataBranch_DoesNotRewindLocalAhead$'`

The actual wording change is:

```go
// preserves an existing local ref when targetHash is already reachable by
// walking back from the local hash ...
// Otherwise (local missing, equal, behind, or diverged) the ref is
// updated to targetHash.
```

If you approve this first change, I’ll make a single commit for it and then move to issue 2.

The comment now reads:

```go
// SafelyAdvanceLocalRef updates localRefName to point at targetHash, except
// when the existing local ref is already at or ahead of targetHash. In that
// case it leaves the local ref unchanged to avoid rewinding locally-ahead
// work. Otherwise (local missing, behind, or diverged) it updates the ref to
// targetHash.
```

It’s in [common.go](/Users/peter/code/devenv/cli/cmd/entire/cli/strategy/common.go:125).

Fresh verification:
- `go test ./cmd/entire/cli -run '^TestFetchMetadataBranch_DoesNotRewindLocalAhead$'`
- `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy -run '^TestFetchV2MainFromURL_DoesNotRewindLocalAhead$|^TestFetchMetadataBranch_DoesNotRewindLocalAhead$'`

If you approve this version, I’ll make the first commit and then move to issue 2.

Committed issue 1 as `docs: clarify SafelyAdvanceLocalRef divergence behavior` (`4babcd63d`).

Next I’ll take issue 2 as a separate patch for your review before committing.
::git-stage{cwd="/Users/peter/code/devenv/cli"}
::git-commit{cwd="/Users/peter/code/devenv/cli"}

